      "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
      "body": "Task 2 is implemented and pushed in signed commit [56e636497c049debe2de5445389abf3e018d4783](https://github.com/Blackcat-Informatics/purrdf/commit/56e636497c049debe2de5445389abf3e018d4783).\n\nGraph, processor, Dataset, ConjunctiveGraph and named-view query callers now route through typed contextual algebra and the existing shared native query plumbing. Graph scope, lazy dataset-required errors, initial binding conversion, configured extensions and duplicate-column Python result access are covered. Ordinary native Store.query, prepared/governed query paths and SHACL retain their existing engine. The implementation is original first-party code: no upstream implementation bodies, runtime RDFLib dependency, new dependency/feature, query-text rewriting or second evaluator were introduced.\n\nValidation: 1,909 affected Rust checks passed; the final focused contextual target passed all 18 tests, including the 241-case frozen matrix, separate BNODE controls, nested-group/projection witnesses, callback order, operational failures and ASK cutoffs. The original frozen vendor failure input also passed through a Rust-only witness with its exact expected row. The rebuilt Python binding passed 14 cases restricted to behavior only Python can exercise: receiver/processor/import dispatch, kwargs, term carriers, exceptions/lifetime and row APIs. Core semantic tests stay in Rust; broad Python scoreboard rows remain explicitly historical snapshots.\n\nIndependent consumer review is PASS. Independent primary native Rust structural-cost review is MET: ordinary parser and evaluator operation/control-flow/frame comparisons preserve native behavior; 27-line untimed layout/allocation/retention/admission/reuse records match the signed baseline byte-for-byte. The ordinary Python host mode is zero-sized; its capture sizes are preserved and its emitted frame is no larger than baseline. No timing benchmark or wasm work was used.\n\nNormal commit hooks passed, the signature verified, and the remote branch reads back the exact full commit ID above. Task 2 implementation and permitted qualification are complete; PR integration remains a separate step.\n",
